    "serverLifetime": "A fresh server for each repetition/variant; all three workloads run in listed order on that server.",
    "http": "Local closed-loop Node fetch clients, Accept-Encoding: identity, full response body consumption, successful 2xx required. No concurrent benchmark was running.",
    "memory": "ps RSS 550 ms after each timed interval, not peak or live-object size. Client and build excluded; native and Node reported separately. Node RSS includes its RSC threads once. Heap used/total are summed across per-isolate snapshots; never sum process.memoryUsage().rss across threads.",
    "instrumentation": "A --require preload in main and RSC isolates samples process.memoryUsage(), v8.getHeapStatistics() and v8.getHeapSpaceStatistics() every 500 ms, and accumulates PerformanceObserver GC events. No forced GC, worker retirement or old-space heap cap.",
    "gc": "GC counts and milliseconds are cumulative since each isolate started, including warmups and previous workloads in the same server. SSR totals include previous API work; Flight totals include API and SSR. Summed GC duration across isolates is not process wall-clock pause time. Snapshot timing can observe different stages of collection.",
    "newSpace": "Measured new_space.space_size was 32 MiB by default, 8 MiB with flag 4, and 16 MiB with flag 8 in both main and RSC isolates. These are the two semispaces of new_space, not all young-generation storage. Node defaults vary with memory limits.",
    "units": "bodyBytes is the mean consumed response bytes per timed request (historical HTML/Flight lengths vary slightly); MiB uses 2^20 bytes; p95Ms and gcMs are milliseconds; repetitions contain unaggregated measurements rounded to three decimals."
  },
  "reproduction": {
    "large": "npm run build:native && node scripts/bench-node-heap.mjs > heap-results.json",
    "smoke": "node scripts/bench-node-heap.mjs --smoke",
    "prerequisites": "Installed repository npm dependencies, release native binary, Node >=22, macOS/Linux ps; NODE_OPTIONS unset.",
    "currentVsHistorical": "The script builds and deletes its own temporary project using the current compiler/runtime. It reproduces the allocation workloads, not old framework source or exact historical response bytes. The light profile is retained as historical context; neither profile is a before/after comparison of the runtime import split."
  },
  "decision": "Keep Node adaptive defaults. A forced 4 MiB semi-space reduced heavy JSON throughput by 15.8% in this run (nonoverlapping three-repetition ranges); 8 MiB was a useful local memory/throughput compromise, not a universal default.",
  "limitations": [
    "Local short microbenchmarks on one host; client and server share CPU. No Next.js or production capacity comparison.",
    "Three repetitions reduce order noise but do not establish statistical confidence or cover all npm workloads.",
    "Smaller semi-spaces may increase promotion/major GC and can yield more resident memory than a larger setting.",
    "Forcing 4 or 8 MiB can increase young-generation size in small containers where Node already chooses a smaller default.",
    "Profiles use different historical runtime snapshots and workload sizes; compare variants within a profile."
  ],
